      "title": "Bound retries and preserve error evidence",
      "eyebrow": "Understand",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "A supplied AWS call needs a finite retry budget and a useful final report, not a loop around every failure.",
          "role": "intro",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#tb1"
            ],
            "fact_ids": []
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "SDK retries cover selected transient or throttling errors; not every failed request is safe to repeat.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Configure the supplied Boto3 client with botocore.config.Config(retries={\"mode\": \"standard\", \"total_max_attempts\": APPROVED_ATTEMPTS}) for bounded SDK backoff. Do not loop around terminal errors.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#f2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Catch botocore.exceptions.ClientError around the supplied call. Inspect response[\"Error\"][\"Code\"] and response[\"Error\"][\"Message\"], retain response[\"ResponseMetadata\"][\"RequestId\"] when present, and report terminal failure or exhausted retries.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#f3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "total_max_attempts includes the initial request; Config max_attempts counts retries after it.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#tb3"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#f4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code_walkthrough",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "from botocore.config import Config\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\nconfig = Config(retries={\"mode\": \"standard\", \"total_max_attempts\": APPROVED_ATTEMPTS})\nclient = supplied_client_setup(config)\ntry:\n    result = supplied_ready_call(client)\nexcept ClientError as error:\n    code = error.response[\"Error\"][\"Code\"]\n    message = error.response[\"Error\"][\"Message\"]\n    request_id = error.response.get(\"ResponseMetadata\", {}).get(\"RequestId\")\n    supplied_report_failure(code, message, request_id)\nelse:\n    supplied_report_success(result)",
          "annotations": [
            {
              "start_line": 4,
              "end_line": 5,
              "text": "Supplied setup and reporting helpers are illustrative. APPROVED_ATTEMPTS=3: 1 initial request plus at most 2 retries; Config max_attempts=3 counts 3 retries after the initial request."
            },
            {
              "start_line": 6,
              "end_line": 7,
              "text": "One application-level call; selected eligible SDK retries use bounded backoff."
            },
            {
              "start_line": 8,
              "end_line": 12,
              "text": "Report terminal failure or exhausted retries with Code, Message and optional RequestId."
            }
          ],
          "reveal": "all",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [],
            "fact_ids": [],
            "anchors": [
              "aws_devops.handle_aws_automation_errors_with_bounded_retries_and_useful_reporting#visual"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "data_table",
          "caption": "SDK attempt-count comparison",
